          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            An atom in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+element"} minimal element
            among those which are not actually the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom+element"} minimum
          %p A related but slightly weaker concept is that of “tiny element”, which has important generalizations in the context of enriched category theory.
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            be a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            (or
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/proset"} proset
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom+element"} bottom element
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+element"} positive
            if it is not a bottom element. An element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is
            %strong atomic
            if, given any element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \leq a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            is positive iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq p
            %strong atom
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is simply an atomic element of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq a
          %p
            The atoms are precisely the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/minimal+elements"} minimal elements
            of the set of positive elements. For a poset,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            is atomic iff every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \leq a
            is positive iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+logic"} classical logic
            too,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            is atomic iff every
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p \leq a
            satisfies
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = \bot
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/xor"} xor
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p = a
          %p
            The p(r)oset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            is
            %strong atomic
            (or more commonly in the literature,
            = succeed ";" do
              %strong atomistic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} supremum
            of atoms. In this case, every element
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            is a supremum of those atoms
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq x
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ⊥
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot
            is a supremum of no atoms, and every atom is a supremum of itself, so the condition is really about the nontrivial nonatomic elements.
          %p
            In
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+element"} positive element
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/predicative+mathematics"} predicative
            constructive mathematics, positivity cannot be defined at all, and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi S
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} S
            must come equipped with a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positivity+predicate"} positivity predicate
            before we may consider its atoms.
          %h3#remarks_on_terminology Remarks on terminology
          %p
            There is some terminological variance in the literature to the notion of atomic poset as defined here. In particular,
            %a{:href => "http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Atom_%28order_theory%29"} Wikipedia
            defines an
            %em atomic poset
            to be a poset in which every positive element has an atom below it, and refers to our stronger notion of atomic poset by the term “atomistic poset”. Note well that the Wikipedia conventions seem to be the ones observed in most lattice-theoretic texts.
          %p
            “Atomic” and “Atomistic” differ for the simple example of the
            %span.newWikiWord
              divisor lattice
              %a{:href => "/nlab/new/divisor+lattice"} ?
            for some number
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semi-atom"} semi-atoms
            which are powers of primes. This lattice is atomic because any object not the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bottom"} bottom
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+arithmetic"} fundamental theorem of arithmetic
            = succeed "." do
              %em unique factorization theorem
          %p
            The two notions coincide in the case of complete Boolean algebras
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is atomic in the Wikipedia sense, and for any element
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b \in B
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi c
                  %mo =
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo ¬
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi atoms
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c = b \wedge \neg (\bigvee \{atoms\, a: a \leq b\})
          %p
            To show
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            is atomistic, it suffices to show
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} c = 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a'
            such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a' \leq c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a' \leq b
            and
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo =
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi a
                  %mo ′
                  %mo ∧
                  %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi atoms
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi b
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a' = a' \wedge a' \leq a' \wedge \bigvee \{atoms\, a: a \leq b\} = 0
          %p
            since
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ′
                    %mo ≤
                    %mo ¬
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi atoms
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a' \leq \neg(\bigvee \{atoms\, a: a \leq b\})
          %p
            Our (
            %em> pro tem
            ) decision to define the word “atomic” in the idiosyncratic nLab sense above is consistent with its use elsewhere in category theory; see the sections below on atomic objects and on categorification.
          %h2#examples Examples
          .num_example
            %h6#example Example
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/power+set"} power set
              the atoms are the
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/singleton+subsets"} singleton subsets
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+boolean+algebra"} complete boolean algebra
              is (up to
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          .num_example
            %h6#example_2 Example
            %p
              In a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice+of+subtoposes"} lattice of subtoposes
              the atoms are the 2-valued
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Boolean+toposes"} Boolean toposes
              = succeed "." do
                %a{:href => "subtopos#BooleantoposesAreAtoms"} this proposition
          %h2#properties Properties
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            is an atom in a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lattice"} lattice
            or more generally a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/meet"} meet
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semilattice"} semilattice
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi b
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            any other element then (using classical logic)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                  %mo ∧
                  %mi b
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mo ⊥
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \wedge b \in \{a, \bot\} .
          %p
            This is simply because
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %mi b
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \wedge b \leq a
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi a
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ⊥
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bot
          %h2#atoms_and_tiny_elements Atoms and tiny elements
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a poset or preorder, in other words a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/enriched+category"} enriched category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in E
            is
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tiny+object"} tiny
            if the hom
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(e, -)\colon E \to \mathbf{2}
            preserves all
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supremum"} sups
            that exist in
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nPOV"} nPOV
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p A tiny element in a Boolean algebra is precisely an atom.
          .proof
            %h6#proof Proof
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              be an atom. Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{x_i\}
              be a collection of elements that admits a supremum such that
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≤
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                        %mi i
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq \bigvee_i x_i
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                      %mi i
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                    %mo =
                    %munder
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⋁
                      %mi i
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = a \wedge \bigvee_i x_i = \bigvee_i a \wedge x_i
            %p
              (where the second equation holds since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \wedge -
              is a left
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjoint+functor"} adjoint
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is a
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Heyting+algebra"} Heyting algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is positive, for some
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
              the element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \wedge x_i
              is positive as well. Trivially it holds that
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∧
                      %msub
                        %mi x
                        %mi i
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi a
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \wedge x_i \leq a
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is an atom, the inequality is an equality. Thus
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %msub
                      %mi x
                      %mi i
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq x_i
              for some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is not an atom, i.e., if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi b
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \lt b \lt a
              for some
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi b
                    %mo ∨
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo ¬
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a = b \vee (a \wedge \neg b)
            %p
              If
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(a, -)
              preserved the join on the right, then either
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq b
              which is evidently false, or
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq a \wedge \neg b
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ≤
                      %mo ¬
                      %mi b
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a \leq \neg b
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∧
                      %mi b
                      %mo ≤
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b = a \wedge b \leq 0
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B(a, -)
              does not preserve suprema.
          %p
            Only one half of this proposition holds (an atom is a tiny element) if we replace the Boolean algebra
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi B
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
            by a general
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/frame"} frame
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+element"} positivity predicate
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
          %p
            Be this as it may,
            %a{:href => "http://www.acsu.buffalo.edu/~wlawvere/ToposMotion.pdf#page=6"} Lawvere
            has written, “In order to settle once and for all the various terminological differences, perhaps we can use a.t.o.m. as an abbreviation for ‘amazing tiny object model’.” This is Lawvere’s ‘objective’ way of abbreviating “atomic object”; the word ‘amazing’ here is presumably chosen to evoke what Lawvere has called the “
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/amazing+right+adjoint"}> amazing right adjoint
            ” to an exponential functor
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-)^D
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/synthetic+differential+geometry"} synthetic differential geometry
            where such adjoints exist for
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinitesimal+object"} infinitesimal objects
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D
          %h2#generalization_and_categorification Generalization and categorification
          %p
            The result that an atomic complete Boolean algebra is isomorphic to a power set – hence to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf"} presheaf
            with values in the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-category"} 0-category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi Grpd
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2} = (-1)Grpd
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28-1%29-groupoid"} (-1)-groupoids
            – may be generalized and categorified as follows.
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            be a
            = succeed "-category," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cosmos"} cosmos
            (a complete, cocomplete, symmetric monoidal closed category). We define an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            to be
            %strong tiny
            or
            %strong atomic
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(e, -) \colon E \to V
            preserves any
            = succeed "-colimit" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/weighted+colimit"} weighted colimit
          %p
            In what follows, we suppose the full
            = succeed "-subcategory" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Tiny
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tiny(E)
            of atomic objects in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is essentially small. The inclusion
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Tiny
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Tiny(E) \hookrightarrow E
            induces a restricted Yoneda embedding
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mi Tiny
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %msup
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E \to V^{Tiny(E)^{op}}
          %p
            sending an object
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(i-, e)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is
            %strong
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/atomic+category"} atomic
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi i
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi Tiny
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ↪
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Tiny(E) \hookrightarrow E
            is
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dense+functor"} dense
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi e
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a canonical colimit of atomic objects below it, in the precise sense that the following enriched
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coend"} coend
            exists, and its canonical map to
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∫
                    %mrow
                      %mi a
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi Tiny
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mi E
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi i
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi i
                  %mi a
                  %mo →
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int^{a \in Tiny(E)} E(i a, e) \cdot i a \to e,
          %p is an isomorphism.
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is a preorder, i.e., is
            = succeed "-enriched" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}
            is the category of
            = succeed "-categories," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (-1)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi sup
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mi i
                  %mi a
                  %mo :
                  %mi i
                  %mi a
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \sup \{i a: i a \leq p\}
          %p
            so that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi E
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
            is atomic precisely if every element is the sup of the tiny elements below it.
          .num_thm
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              A small-cocomplete atomic preorder
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is equivalent to the free sup-lattice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{T^{op}}
              generated by the preorder
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo =
                    %mi Tiny
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T = Tiny(E)
              of tiny elements. Conversely, every free sup-lattice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{T^{op}}
              is small-cocomplete and atomic, where
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is the poset of tiny elements.
          %p
            N.B. “Free sup-lattice” refers to a left adjoint of the forgetful functor
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi SupLat
                  %mo →
                  %mi Preord
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U \colon SupLat \to Preord
            from sup-lattices to preorders.
          .proof
            %h6#proof_2 Proof
            %p
              Since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is cocomplete, and since
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mi Tiny
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}^{Tiny(E)^{op}}
              is the free sup-lattice or cocomplete preorder generated from
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Tiny
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi E
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Tiny(E)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi i
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Tiny
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \colon Tiny(E) \to E
              extends uniquely to a sup-preserving map
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %mi Tiny
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %msup
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \colon \mathbf{2}^{Tiny(E)^{op}} \to E
            %p
              which sends
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mi Tiny
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi E
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X \colon Tiny(E)^{op} \to \mathbf{2}
              to
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mrow
                        %mi a
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi Tiny
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi E
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi i
                    %mi a
                    %mo =
                    %mi sup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                    %mi i
                    %mi a
                    %mo :
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int^{a \in Tiny(E)} X(a) \cdot i a = \sup \{i a: X(a) = 1\}.
            %p
              This
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is left adjoint to the restricted Yoneda embedding
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi R
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                      %mi E
                      %mo →
                      %msup
                        %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                          %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mi Tiny
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi E
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} R \colon E \to \mathbf{2}^{Tiny(E)^{op}}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is atomic says that for each
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi e
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi E
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e \in E
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv R
              at
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi e
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} e
              is an isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∫
                      %mi a
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi e
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⋅
                    %mi i
                    %mi a
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi e
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \int^a E(i a, e) \cdot i a \cong e.
            %p
              On the other hand, the value of the unit of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊣
                    %mi R
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \dashv R
              at an object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is given by a string of isomorphisms
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi X
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo ≅
                              %mi Yoneda
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ∫
                              %mi a
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi Tiny
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≅
                          %mtd
                            %msup
                              %mo ∫
                              %mi a
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo −
                            %mo ,
                            %mi i
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo ≅
                          %mtd
                            %mi E
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi i
                            %mo −
                            %mo ,
                            %msup
                              %mo ∫
                              %mi a
                            %mi X
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mo ⋅
                            %mi i
                            %mi a
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    X &amp; \stackrel{Yoneda}{\cong} &amp; \int^a X(a) \cdot Tiny(E)(-, a) \\
                    \&amp; \cong &amp; \int^a X(a) \cdot E(i-, i a) \\
                    \&amp; \cong &amp; E(i-, \int^a X(a) \cdot i a)
                    }
            %p
              where the last isomorphism obtains from the fact that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E(i a, -)
              preserves colimits if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi a
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} a
              is tiny. Thus the unit is also an isomorphism.
            %p
              For the converse: each representable object
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi t
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T(-, t)
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                        %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2}^{T^{op}}
              is tiny, because the covariant functor
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi T
                            %mi op
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi T
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo ,
                      %mi t
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo ,
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{T^{op}}(T(-, t), -)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
              by the Yoneda lemma, preserves colimits. Furthermore, every functor
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo :
                    %msup
                      %mi T
                      %mi op
                    %mo →
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X: T^{op} \to \mathbf{2}
              is a canonical colimit of representables, so that
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mn 2
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi T
                          %mi op
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{T^{op}}
              is atomic in addition to being cocomplete.
          .num_cor
            %h6#corollary Corollary
            %p
              A complete atomic Boolean algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi B
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
              is isomorphic to
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mi T
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^T
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi T
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} T
              is the discrete preorder of atoms of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi B
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} B
          %p
            The argument given for the theorem above carries over without obstruction to the general enriched setting. In particular, replacing
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mstyle{:mathvariant => "bold"}
                      %mn 2
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbf{2} = (-1)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Cat
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
            by its categorification
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Set
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set = 0
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Cat
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Cat
          .num_thm
            %h6#theorem_bunge Theorem (Bunge)
            %p
              A category
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi E
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} E
              is equivalent to a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/presheaf+topos"} presheaf topos
              (functors with values in the 1-category
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Set"} Set
              of
              = succeed ")" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/0-groupoids"} 0-groupoids
              = succeed "-category." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Set
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi C
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo ,
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} C(-, c)
              are (among the) atomic objects of
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi Set
                        %mrow
                          %msup
                            %mi C
                            %mi op
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{C^{op}}
          %p
            (The literal statement in Bunge’s thesis is that a category is equivalent to a presheaf category
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi Set
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi C
                        %mi op
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Set^{C^{op}}
            if and only if it is cocomplete, regular, and has a generating set of atomic objects, but this is trivially the same since presheaf toposes are of course
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/regular+category"} regular
